OL,3,GNEWSAResidents and officials meet on
OL,4,Adredging concerns
OL,5,
OL,6,FHarbour officials have agreed to meet
OL,7,Fwith residents who are worried about
OL,8,Fsand and silt from dredging being left
OL,9,Fon a beach.
OL,11,FLetters from 24 people were sent to the
OL,12,FGovernment of Jersey's environment
OL,13,Fdepartment claiming dredging at St
OL,14,FAubin could harm wildlife and be a
OL,15,Fdanger to people.
OL,17,FMinister for Environment Mary Le
OL,18,FHegarat said: "Officers will look to
OL,19,Fmeet with a complainant in the coming
OL,20,Fdays and review the situation before
OL,21,Freporting back to me so of a course an
OL,22,Faction can be decided."
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
